### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  Library REST API — Demo
###  Generated from docs/experiments/examples/library-checkout.poly
###
###  Start the server:
###    dotnet run --project demo/Poly.RestApi --urls "http://localhost:5201"
###
###  Then click "Send Request" above any request below.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ──────────── BOOKS ────────────

### List all books
GET http://localhost:5201/api/books

### Get book by ISBN
GET http://localhost:5201/api/books/978-0441172719

### Create a new book (validates constraints: ISBN length 10-17, Pages 1-10000, required fields)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Snow Crash",
    "author": "Neal Stephenson",
    "isbn": "978-0553380958",
    "pages": 440,
    "genre": 0
}

### Create a book with invalid ISBN (too short — expect 409 with validation error)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Bad Book",
    "author": "Test Author",
    "isbn": "123",
    "pages": 100,
    "genre": 0
}

### ──────────── PATRONS ────────────

### List all patrons
GET http://localhost:5201/api/patrons

### Get patron by email
GET http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/alice@library.org

### Register a new patron (validates: email pattern, Name required, MaxItems 0-20)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Carol White",
    "email": "carol@library.org",
    "maxItems": 10,
    "currentBorrowCount": 0,
    "outstandingFines": null
}

### Register a patron with invalid email (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Bad Email",
    "email": "not-an-email",
    "maxItems": 5,
    "currentBorrowCount": 0,
    "outstandingFines": null
}

### ──────────── ACTIONS (Stage- & Policy-Guarded) ────────────

### CheckOut: Bob borrows Dune (should succeed — Bob is Active, good standing)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "isbn": "978-0441172719"
}

### CheckOut: Bob borrows a second book (should succeed)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "isbn": "978-0441569595"
}

### CheckOut: Bob tries a third (should fail — AtLimit policy, MaxItems is 3 but loans could be 2)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "isbn": "978-0465026562"
}

### Suspend: Bob (should succeed — is Active, not AtLimit)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/suspend

### CheckOut: Bob after suspend (should fail — stage guard: requires Active)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "isbn": "978-0465026562"
}

### Reinstate: Bob (will fail with NotSupportedException — HasOverdueLoans uses Q3′ any-quantifier)
POST http://localhost:5201/api/patrons/bob@library.org/reinstate

### ──────────── LOANS ────────────

### List all loans
GET http://localhost:5201/api/loans

### ──────────── EXPECTED FLOW ────────────
###  1. GET /api/books                          → 200, 3 books
###  2. POST /api/patrons/bob/checkout (Dune)   → 200, Loan returned
###  3. POST /api/patrons/bob/checkout (N'man)  → 200, Loan returned
###  4. POST /api/patrons/bob/suspend           → 200, { status: "suspended" }
###  5. POST /api/patrons/bob/checkout (Gödel)  → 409, requires stage Active
###  6. POST /api/patrons/bob/reinstate         → 500 (Q3′ not supported yet)
###  7. GET /api/loans                          → 200, 2 loans
